{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_j2zyza4jckmifgzvn4g4isjbj3dhxl6v3u5m4bqdpun35dspt4sa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **All four phases pass; two real bugs found and fixed in the Rust.**\n\n## Bugs found & fixed in `translation/src/lib.rs`\n\n**1. Struct padding dropped on element moves** (caught by `CONFIGS.md` row 17)\ngcc compiles the C `b[k] = a[i]` as a full 16-byte move — it copies the struct's 4 trailing padding bytes. Rust's `*dst = *src` on the `#[repr(C)]` struct copied only the two fields, leaving the destination's padding intact. Observable to any caller reading the buffers as bytes. Fixed by moving elements through a `[u8; 16]` temporary (also correct when `src == dst`).\n\n**2. `memcpy` approximated rather than called** (caught by `ERRORS.md` rows 2/7/8/10/12)\nRust used `ptr::copy_nonoverlapping` with a hand-written `if bytes != 0 && a != b` guard. That guard changed behavior for `a == b == NULL, size > 0` (C faults, Rust returned), and could not reproduce glibc's argument-dependent strategy selection for huge counts. Fixed by declaring and calling libc `memcpy` directly, exactly as the C does.\n\n## Notable finding: the crash rows are not naively testable\nFor negative/huge `size`, the C computes a ~2^64 byte count. Its **own** outcome is layout-dependent — same `size`, different buffer address, and the C alone flips between `Exited(0)` and `SIGSEGV`. A \"did both crash?\" assertion would test the process layout, not the translation. Instead each such row runs both `.so`s on **identical addresses** inside a 4 KiB window centred in a 256 MiB `PROT_NONE` reservation, with a `SIGSEGV` handler capturing `si_addr`, and asserts the **exact faulting address** matches — proving both passed identical `(dst, src, n)` to `memcpy`. All addresses match exactly (e.g. `size=-1` → `0x…fffffb0` in both).\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff empty, 0 unresolved non-libc symbols | ✅ (`merge_sort` only; 3 `static` helpers translated, correctly unexported) |\n| Phase B — all 20 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass, randomized | ✅ 21 tests + ~322k randomized stress trials |\n| Binary stdout comparison | ✅ N/A — no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]` |\n| Phase C — all 12 `ERRORS.md` rows pass | ✅ 12 tests, each asserted non-vacuous |\n| Every feature combination | ✅ no `[features]` declared; default + `--no-default-features` × **release + debug** `.so` = 4 configs, all green |\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `verify.sh` (one-command re-verification), and `tests/{common,phase_b_configs,phase_c_errors,phase_d_symbols,stress_random}`. Both libraries are always loaded via `libloading` and called through their exported symbols. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":574,"cache_read_input_tokens":165757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":574,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62db9202-04ec-4326-944d-d3d0b591b984","uuid":"1c80aa6f-471a-410d-b4ea-48d290707bb2","timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:39:04.348Z"}
